Title: Capture one merged PR's review attribution in one call
Created: 2026-10-27
Author: reviewer

--- log ---
2026-10-27T09:27Z reviewer created

--- body ---
## Context
Roar's capture runbook (`skills/roar/runbooks/capture.md`) chains three
`scripts/attribution_record.py` modes by hand for every reviewed merged PR:
`--seats-pr`, then `--extract --merged <date>`, then `--capture`. The merge
date has to be looked up, and a seat failure part-way leaves the operator to
work out what to redo. The author called the post-merge extraction and
capture burdensome (2026-10-27 discussion); 43 commits in the two weeks
before mention attribution.

## Scope
Add `--capture-pr N` running the three in order, with the merge date read
from the forge. Storage location unchanged; moving the record out of
journal files is ticket 1243.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] `--capture-pr N --capture PROJECT --audience A` captures a merged PR's block with its forge merge date
- [ ] An unmerged PR is refused before any body edit
- [ ] A seat failure captures nothing; a rerun after the fix captures once, without duplicating seats
- [ ] The capture runbook names the one call as the common path
- [ ] `make check` passes
